 "notes": "A vira-lata caramelo: slim build, medium drop ears, slim muzzle, light chest, sickle tail curled over the back. Every clip is built from keyframes drawn by hand at native size in pets/species/caramelo/keys/*.txt. look-up-left is the target pose: sitting, muzzle raised toward the person, ear hanging back, tail curled over the back (use it when the owner is near). Loops are one keyframe plus what moves: the side walk alternates two strides with a passing frame where the body rises 1 px, the front and back walks lift the legs in turn, resting poses breathe, happy and wag move only the tail, look-down slides the eyes, beg raises the paws, the run goes reach, flight, gather, contact. Coat patterns are regions of their own: ear and earpatch (malhado carries one caramel ear, the same ear from every side), patch (malhado saddle and hip), tan (brows and lower legs of the preto-caramelo), blaze (the caramelo forehead stripe, tail tip and belly). Extra clips: wag-down, run-left, carry-left (jaw open, the runtime draws the ball at the muzzle), sniff-left, sniff-down, beg-down, bark-down, blink-down. One-shots (loop false): stretch-left (play bow), pounce-left, yawn-down, blink-down. happy-down is the petting reaction.",
